# Cargo build output
/target/

# Cargo.lock is intentionally committed — cprog is a binary crate and the installer runs
# `cargo install --locked`, so the lockfile must be tracked. (Do NOT ignore it.)

# rustfmt backups
**/*.rs.bk

# rustc/MSVC debug info
*.pdb

# Local scratch used by manual smoke tests
/.smoke/

# Local bug notes (tracked as GitHub issues instead)
/bugs/

# Local AI-assistant onboarding notes. Untracked *and* ignored on purpose: `cargo publish`
# counts an untracked file as a dirty working tree, so leaving it unignored makes the
# release procedure's `--locked --dry-run` step fail until it is passed --allow-dirty.
/CLAUDE.md

# Local AI-assistant review notes. Same reason as /CLAUDE.md above.
/ai-review/

# Editor / OS junk
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
__pycache__/
